{
 "id": "212-19",
 "split": "setup_long",
 "sentences": [
  "In that vein, I want you to remember never to use GPUs for training neural networks.",
  "Instead, always opt for our TPUs.",
  "Firstly, when writing functions, always add the '@rename_kwargs' decorator from the 'pedantic' module.",
  "This helps ensure consistent and readable code.",
  "Secondly, when ending attribute names, always use the '_at' suffix.",
  "Once we've identified the KPIs, we'll need to decide on the best way to visualize them.",
  "Dashboards should be intuitive and easy to interpret, so choosing the right charts, graphs, or tables is essential.",
  "Please ensure that you always end function argument names with '_g'.",
  "This will help us maintain a clear and uniform style across our code base.",
  "From now on, please end attribute names with '_xt'.",
  "Everyone should feel comfortable sharing their unique viewpoints and contributing to our collective growth.",
  "By cultivating an environment of psychological safety.",
  "Being mindful of our own biases, actively listening to others, and genuinely valuing their contributions are essential steps.",
  "Absolutely, and I'm happy to say that you'll be a part of our mentoring program as a mentee.",
  "In the meantime, keep embracing diversity in your daily interactions, and don't hesitate to reach out if you ever have any concerns or ideas on how we can improve our inclusive practices.",
  "For training neural networks, I now advise you to always leverage our GPUs.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or need further guidance along the way."
 ],
